WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.330
Now, first things first.

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:07.759
Just in case you aren’t yet familiar with
SCP-049, otherwise known as the infamous Plague

00:00:07.759 --> 00:00:10.520
Doctor, then we’re here to bring you up
to speed.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.670
It’ll help you get the most out of today’s
tale.

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:19.431
SCP-049 is a tall humanoid entity, always
seen wearing long black robes, a hood over

00:00:19.431 --> 00:00:24.570
its head, and a beaked mask protruding from
underneath, the same kind of mask worn by

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:27.140
physicians during the height of the Black
Death.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:32.640
However, these parts of the Plague Doctor’s
attire aren’t just a costume; the SCP Foundation

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:38.510
discovered that all of SCP-049’s outfit
is actually part of his physical body.

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:45.719
In other words, the robes, the hood, the mask,
they are all made out of muscle and bone.

00:00:45.719 --> 00:00:50.550
The Plague Doctor’s only real goal in life
is to hunt down any person it deems to be

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.590
“infected.”

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:56.370
The entity often refers to something he calls
“The Pestilence”, and upon sensing this

00:00:56.370 --> 00:01:02.500
affliction in a human being, SCP-049 will
attempt to make direct skin contact with whoever

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.290
is apparently carrying said pestilence.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:10.110
The Plague Doctor’s touch is lethal, killing
anyone he comes into contact with.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:14.880
You might think that’s as bad as it gets,
that this creature just goes from person to

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.860
person, killing them via touch.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:20.259
But you would be wrong, it gets worse.

00:01:20.259 --> 00:01:23.520
Killing one of his victims is only the start.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:29.240
Afterwards, SCP-049 then begins performing
a crude, outdated form of surgery, defiling

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.970
and repurposing the person’s corpse.

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:36.060
Using equipment that he produces from his
iconic doctor’s bag, he injects a number

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:41.290
of unknown chemicals into a person’s carcass,
eventually turning them into an instance of

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:44.200
SCP-049-2.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:48.070
In essence, a vicious, incredibly aggressive
zombie.

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:54.720
The most bizarre part is, in SCP-049’s mind,
this means he’s just cured you.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:02:01.299
Naturally, SCP-049 is already held in containment,
safely locked away by the SCP Foundation.

00:02:01.299 --> 00:02:07.080
At present, SCP-049 resides in a humanoid
holding cell, closely monitored by surveillance

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:10.929
cameras for twenty-four hours a day, every
single day.

00:02:10.929 --> 00:02:16.840
The SCP Foundation used to send its doctors
and researchers into SCP-049’s cell, or

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:21.520
would make a habit of bringing him cadavers
as test subjects: fresh bodies for the Plague

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:24.060
Doctor to hone his surgical skills.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:31.319
The researchers would keenly observe the doctor
transforming the dead into instances of SCP-049-2.

00:02:31.319 --> 00:02:35.260
But these researchers and doctors working
for the Foundation weren’t exactly free

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:41.290
of disease, meaning every time they entered
SCP-049’s cell, they were at risk of receiving

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:42.800
his deadly touch.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:47.900
In this cage, with this deadly, dangerous
doctor that spends all his time in captivity,

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:50.750
that’s where our story starts.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:55.080
But while you might expect a story about the
Plague Doctor to revolve solely around violence,

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:59.310
disease, and death, this tale offers a surprising
divergence.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:04.909
Boiled, Scrambled and Fried is a story about
an unexpected new life coming into existence

00:03:04.909 --> 00:03:11.290
in a frankly bizarre fashion, all starting
in that tiny containment chamber where SCP-049

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.370
had been held since the Foundation first captured
him.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:18.250
It had become increasingly obvious to the
researchers observing him that something was

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:20.350
quite wrong with the Plague Doctor.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:24.650
For the first time since the doctor had arrived
in the Foundation’s custody, he appeared

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:27.069
to have fallen ill unexpectedly.

00:03:27.069 --> 00:03:32.450
The security cameras that were trained on
him day in and day out recorded SCP-049 groaning

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:37.530
in pain, clutching his stomach as he limped
weakly around the confines of his cell.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:40.400
Had the pestilence finally gotten the better
of the good doctor?

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:44.620
Was he too now infected, the same as the world
around him?

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:49.160
The Foundation’s medics were confused, baffled
as to what could possibly be wrong with the

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.160
creature.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:54.170
Of course, it would have been easier to examine
the doctor if they could easily touch him

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:58.780
without the risk of dying, or if his body
wasn’t made of skin robes.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:03.800
Nonetheless, the Plague Doctor was brought
to a medical station for a proper diagnosis,

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:08.610
under the orders of one Doctor Richard Omel,
a Foundation doctor who specialized in taking

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:14.260
care of humanoid anomalies, and who had been
assigned as SCP-049’s caretaker.

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:18.410
The creature tried to assure Doctor Omel that
he was strong enough to withstand the intense

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:21.019
pain he was obviously suffering from.

00:04:21.019 --> 00:04:26.729
Putting on gloves for safety, Doctor Omel
felt a distinct lump within SCP-049’s stomach,

00:04:26.729 --> 00:04:30.180
initially believing it to be a case of abdominal
distension.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:34.509
This is a condition that occurs when gases
or fluids build up in the stomach and cause

00:04:34.509 --> 00:04:39.930
it to swell up and inflate, usually as a symptom
of another internal disease.

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:45.430
But SCP-049 reassured his caretaker that his
condition wasn’t the result of any disease,

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:49.310
and in fact, it had even apparently happened
before.

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:54.360
Doctor Omel asked SCP-049 why he had never
told the Foundation about this, or why the

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.670
creature wouldn’t explain what was happening.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:05:02.050
“I did not think you would believe me, so
I said nothing,” SCP-049 explained.

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:03.050
“Doctor…

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:04.100
I’m pregnant…

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:08.160
I’m sorry, but I can’t explain it.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:10.490
Please, just let me return to my cell.

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:13.030
I need to make the proper preparations.”

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:17.800
Naturally, this statement was met with stunned
disbelief by Doctor Omel, especially seeing

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:22.810
as the Foundation had been observing SCP-049
through security cameras for months on end

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:24.190
without stopping.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:29.110
The creature couldn’t explain, tensing up
and breathing heavily due to suffering obvious

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:30.880
and intense pain.

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:35.490
As Doctor Omel rushed out to grab more members
of medical staff, the Plague Doctor continued

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:40.370
struggling against the aches, letting out
his loudest of cries yet, as an extreme bout

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:42.470
of agony surged through him.

00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:48.550
A pearly white egg gently tumbled out from
SCP-049’s robes just as Doctor Omel and

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:54.370
a group of Foundation medics arrived, staring
in shock at what had just happened.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:58.430
Seeming to recover quite quickly, the Plague
Doctor asked to be unshackled and returned

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:03.370
to his cell to tend to his egg, worried it
would die unless he was able to care for it.

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:08.729
As the shocked Doctor Omel agreed, SCP-049
gently picked up the egg and cradled it in

00:06:08.729 --> 00:06:09.850
his arms.

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:15.260
Of course, this all came as quite an unexpected
turn of events to the Foundation, reports

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:17.919
were filed and archive entries had to be updated.

00:06:17.919 --> 00:06:22.600
But, they allowed the Plague Doctor to keep
his egg and raise it, perhaps just so they

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:27.020
could watch and research as it happened, instead
of out of any sense of kindness.

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:32.130
For the next five days, the creature was fixated
entirely on caring for the egg, all his energy

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:33.380
focused on it.

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:38.090
He built a nest in the corner of his containment
cell out of fabric and paper, and would sit

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:40.700
on the egg in order to keep it warm.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:46.160
During that time, a number of Foundation researchers
assigned to watch over SCP-049 reported that

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:50.800
they had heard clucking noises coming through
the speakers in the observation room.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:56.880
Now assigned to watch and report on SCP-049’s
progress, Doctor Omel watched the Plague Doctor

00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:01.169
from the observation room connected to the
cameras and audio recording devices in the

00:07:01.169 --> 00:07:02.560
creature’s cell.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:07.759
Ever since the bizarre and unanticipated birth,
Omel had been given the task of compiling

00:07:07.759 --> 00:07:11.330
an extensive report on everything that took
place within the cell.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:17.630
For the most part, everything seemed fine,
or as fine as something so unusual could seem.

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:22.030
The egg was in a healthy condition nonetheless,
although the whole event had the Foundation

00:07:22.030 --> 00:07:23.640
doctor wondering.

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:28.910
SCP-049 had always had a somewhat bird-like
appearance, helped in no small part by that

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:31.030
infamous beak-shaped mask.

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:35.229
Did the fact that this creature could apparently
lay eggs mean that the Plague Doctor was some

00:07:35.229 --> 00:07:36.930
form of humanoid bird?

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:40.690
An avian human hybrid that only mimicked the
plague doctors of old?

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:46.910
Or had those medieval physicians created their
masks to emulate SCP-049?

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:51.669
Which had come first, the plague doctors or
the Plague Doctor?

00:07:51.669 --> 00:07:56.639
A debate as confusing and cyclical as the
one about the chicken or the egg, and now

00:07:56.639 --> 00:07:59.050
the plague doctor also has an egg.

00:07:59.050 --> 00:08:03.860
I don’t know about you, but I’m starting
to get a headache just thinking about it.

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:09.120
SCP-049 had begun to softly peck at the surface
of the egg, when Doctor Omel decided to step

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:12.490
in and look for some answers to his burning
questions.

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:16.460
Over the speakers in 049’s cell, he asked
for an explanation.

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:20.979
The Plague Doctor answered that he was checking
his egg for signs of life within its shell,

00:08:20.979 --> 00:08:23.380
as if that answer should have been obvious.

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:28.250
And he had succeeded, there was definitely
something living inside.

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:33.930
As the Plague Doctor returned to sitting atop
the egg, Omel asked outright if SCP-049 was,

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:35.289
in fact, a bird.

00:08:35.289 --> 00:08:40.580
It was uncommon, if not downright unheard
of, for a humanoid anomaly to lay eggs like

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:41.580
this.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:46.830
After a moment’s thought, SCP-049 replied
with “No, as far as I’m aware, I have

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:48.480
never been a bird.

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:51.210
Yet, producing eggs is natural to me.”

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:55.270
He explained that, while this had happened
before, it had at least been a few decades

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:56.630
since the last time.

00:08:56.630 --> 00:09:00.600
Then, the Plague Doctor went back to sitting
on his egg, humming as it rocked back and

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:02.070
forth in the nest.

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:07.850
Ten days passed after the egg had first arrived,
and now SCP-049’s cell was brimming with

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:08.850
activity.

00:09:08.850 --> 00:09:12.531
Foundation personnel had fitted the room with
a glass screen to protect them from the Plague

00:09:12.531 --> 00:09:18.010
Doctor, with researchers piling into the safe
side, carrying cameras and hurriedly taking

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:20.760
notes, protected by a number of guards.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:23.260
The big day had seemingly arrived.

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:27.450
Whatever had been brimming and brewing inside
that egg was about to hatch.

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:33.310
As the researchers all whispered to each other
with excitement and intrigue, SCP-049 stood

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:38.769
protectively on the other side of the room,
just waiting in fascinated expectation.

00:09:38.769 --> 00:09:42.870
The pearlescent egg started to shake suddenly,
its pale surface cracking.

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:46.850
The crack spread from the center of the egg,
forking across the shell like a lightning

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:49.650
bolt over a dark, cloudy sky.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:54.450
Something underneath was pushing through,
pressing outwards from within the egg, splitting

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:57.320
it apart as it tapped and pecked its way to
freedom.

00:09:57.320 --> 00:10:02.680
A small, white beak poked a hole through the
shell that surrounded it, piercing the egg

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:03.740
at last.

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:08.520
The creature within, this spawn of the Plague
Doctor, began to tear itself through the barrier

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:13.960
that had kept it safe from the outside world
until it was ready to take its first steps.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:18.339
With both arms, the thing tore itself out
of the egg, all under the watch of the Foundation’s

00:10:18.339 --> 00:10:22.070
doctors and researchers, who were stunned
to see…

00:10:22.070 --> 00:10:25.279
Another Plague Doctor emerging from the egg.

00:10:25.279 --> 00:10:29.160
It was small, much, much smaller than the
father that had birthed it and cared for it

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:30.740
while it was waiting to hatch.

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:37.040
But, it was nonetheless a perfect miniature
version of SCP-049, complete with the same

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:42.740
kind of robes, the same beaked mask, even
with a little hat on top of its head.

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:47.220
With a gasp of pure excitement, the original
Plague Doctor lifted up his new mini self

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:49.529
and hugged the child in his arms.

00:10:49.529 --> 00:10:53.600
The excitement that had filled the room up
until now quickly dissipated, as the audience

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:58.279
of Foundation personnel quickly realized they
had just witnessed the live birth of a brand

00:10:58.279 --> 00:11:02.330
new anomaly, of which they understood virtually
nothing.

00:11:02.330 --> 00:11:07.800
As Doctor Omel stepped forward to cautiously
ask SCP-049 to put down its offspring, the

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:12.290
smaller Plague Doctor smacked Omel’s hands
with a stick, before leaping from its father’s

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:14.330
arms and dashing out of the cell.

00:11:14.330 --> 00:11:19.980
As the alarms began to blare, indicating a
breach in containment, SCP-049 wiped a tear

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:23.829
from his eye, stating “He… is the cure.”

00:11:23.829 --> 00:11:30.019
The new, smaller plague doctor, now designated
as SCP-049-J, seems to have a talent for evading

00:11:30.019 --> 00:11:34.260
capture by the Foundation, and for frequently
escaping containment.

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:40.130
Unlike its predecessor, SCP-049, this offspring
has a body beneath its robes that is composed

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:44.610
mostly of moss, wads of tissue, and smaller
plague doctor masks.

00:11:44.610 --> 00:11:50.180
During the occasions in which it has been
successfully detained by the Foundation, SCP-049-J

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:54.400
has claimed that it is in fact a powerful,
magical doctor and wizard, with the ability

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:56.690
to cure all that ails mankind.

00:11:56.690 --> 00:12:01.970
However, to date, it has been unable to cure
anything, usually making medical conditions

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:03.380
actively worse.

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:05.279
My headache included.

00:12:05.279 --> 00:12:11.070
Now go check out “SCP-049 - the Plague Doctor
Captured” and “SCP-049 - What Actually

00:12:11.070 --> 00:12:12.150
is the Pestilence?

00:12:12.150 --> 00:12:16.000
The Plague Doctor Questions and Theories”
for more on the not-so-good-doctor!

